# TSan suppressions for tools/test-linux.sh --sanitize tsan (#365). Only proven foreign noise (Qt, Mesa, .NET runtime,
# libc), every entry with a comment why. Never suppress frames from libvlqt.so.
# Matching: race:/deadlock: suppress a report if any frame of its stacks lies in the named module; called_from_lib:
# only ignores interceptor calls made from inside the named module. Inside dotnet gcc 13's TSan does not symbolize
# (all frames `<null>`, symbolize.py does it afterwards), so only module names match here.
# Uninstrumented code (dotnet, Qt, Mesa) only shows up via interceptors (malloc/free, pthread_*); its own atomics and
# futexes are invisible to TSan.

# .NET runtime: its pthread mutexes (PAL critical sections, GC/JIT locks) are taken in orders TSan cannot see as safe
# (2670 reports in one resources run, all frames libcoreclr.so; the report flood alone stalled QtNative's workers).
deadlock:libcoreclr.so
# .NET runtime: new/delete between runtime threads (".NET Tiered Com" vs main), synchronised by the runtime's own
# atomics/managed locks that TSan does not see. No libvlqt frame in either stack.
race:libcoreclr.so
# Mesa llvmpipe (libgallium, WSLg/CI without GPU): main thread destroys a mutex/condvar its llvmpipe-N worker threads
# use; Mesa joins them through its own futex-based primitives, which TSan cannot see. Both accesses inside Mesa.
race:libgallium-*.so
# QtCore: QMutex/QWaitCondition/QThread are futex based in the uninstrumented QtCore, so every happens-before inside
# QtCore is invisible and race reports with an access made by QtCore interceptors are false positives by
# construction. Seen: QQmlThread's QDaemonThread allocated on the main thread (vlqt::Scene::create -> QQmlEngine),
# freed by the thread itself at exit. called_from_lib (not race:) ignores only interceptor calls (new/delete, memmove,
# pthread_*) made from inside QtCore; accesses by instrumented libvlqt code stay checked, so QtNative races between its
# own threads (std::mutex/std::atomic, resources.cpp) or on Qt objects are not hidden.
called_from_lib:libQt6Core.so.6
# QtQml: same reason, the QML type loader hands QML data blobs from the main thread (QQmlTypeLoader::doLoad, under
# vlqt::Scene::create) to its QQmlThread (QQmlJS::Parser frees them) via QtCore's invisible locks/event queue.
# called_from_lib as for QtCore. Deliberately per module (not libQt6*), each module named explicitly.
called_from_lib:libQt6Qml.so.6
# QtGui: QImage::convertToFormat (convertPixels, image_resource.cpp) splits large images into segments on
# QGuiApplication's QThreadPool and waits on a QSemaphore; the segment runnable is new'ed in the calling thread (QtNative
# decode worker) and deleted in the pool worker. Reproduced without any QtNative code (4 std::threads calling
# convertToFormat: same addresses libQt6Gui+0x1abe40 new / +0x1aaf0c delete). called_from_lib as for QtCore.
called_from_lib:libQt6Gui.so.6
